    "content": `## Executive Threat Summary

A critical path delimiter discrepancy has been uncovered across several tier-1 Content Delivery Networks (CDNs). When dynamic single-page applications utilize relaxed routing engines, an attacker can trick edge caches into storing confidential authenticated responses under static file extensions.

> **KEY FINDING**: Semicolons (\`;\`) and URL-encoded delimiters (\`%2F\`) are discarded by backend microservices while being evaluated as file extensions by intermediate CDN proxies.

![Figure 2: Edge caching proxy cluster topology.](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=1200)

---

## Technical Discrepancy Breakdown

### Edge Proxy vs Origin Server Delimiter Processing

| Delimiter | Edge Proxy Interpretation | Origin Server Interpretation | Resulting Vulnerability |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| \`/user/data.css\` | Static CSS Asset | Dynamic User Route | Web Cache Deception |
| \`/api;debug=true\` | Strips Query Parameters | Executes Debug Routine | Authorization Bypass |
| \`%2e%2e%2f\` | Normalizes Path | Resolves Local File | Path Traversal |

---

## Raw HTTP Exploit Request

\`\`\`http
GET /myaccount/financial-summary.css HTTP/1.1
Host: enterprise.wondercave.com
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0
Cookie: session_auth=token_valid_998811
Accept: text/css,*/*;q=0.1
\`\`\`

The CDN edge stores the HTTP 200 response containing credit balances for 2 hours. The attacker subsequently visits the identical URL without cookies and retrieves the victim's private records.

### Hardened Proxy Configuration Pattern

\`\`\`nginx
# Hardened NGINX / Cloudflare Worker Caching Policy
location / {
    # Mandate strict Cache-Control evaluation
    proxy_ignore_headers X-Accel-Expires;
    proxy_pass http://backend_pool;
    
    # Strip caching for any endpoint returning user session cookies
    if ($http_cookie ~* "session|token|auth") {
        set $no_cache 1;
    }
    proxy_no_cache $no_cache;
    proxy_cache_bypass $no_cache;
}
\`\`\`

![Figure 3: Cache status header inspection showing HIT for private user payload.](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=1200)

---

## Defense-in-Depth Checklist

1. **Emit Cache-Control: no-store**: All authenticated endpoints must explicitly emit strict anti-caching headers.
2. **Validate Content-Type before Caching**: CDNs must verify that responses claiming to be \`.css\` actually return \`Content-Type: text/css\`.
3. **Isolate Static Hostnames**: Move public static files to separate subdomains (e.g. \`assets.wondercave.com\`).`
